      "content_summary": "Explains how to mitigate slow response times and throttling errors when capacity limits are reached, focusing on manual configuration adjustments and infrastructure scaling.",
      "content_body": "When observing symptoms like 'Rate Limit Exceeded' or 'Throttling', check if the current infrastructure capacity matches the traffic load. Historically, this was resolved by manually increasing server instances or adjusting rate limit headers in the gateway configuration, as autoscaling policies often failed to trigger quickly enough under sudden spikes. Ensure that memory usage metrics are monitored to prevent data loss during forced scale-downs. If rate limit misconfiguration is suspected, verify that the quota settings align with the service agreement rather than the default low-capacity limits."
